When connecting to the same device with both Bluetooth Classic and Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE), you need to specify the protocol to use to avoid confusion with another device.

In this case, you can use the `BTM` (Bluetooth Management) protocol to switch between Bluetooth Classic and BLE modes.

Here are the steps:

1. Establish a connection with the device using Bluetooth Classic.
2. Use the `BTM_SetMode` command to switch to BLE mode. You can specify the address of the device you want to connect to using the `BTM_DeviceID` parameter.
3. The device will switch to BLE mode and the connection will be established using BLE.

Here is an example code snippet in C++:
```c
#include <bluetooth.h>

int main() {
    // Establish Bluetooth Classic connection
    bluetoothing_t bt_device;
    bluetoothing_init(&bt_device);
    bluetoothing_connect(&bt_device, "Device Name", NULL);

    // Switch to BLE mode
    bt_device.mode = BTM_BLE_MODE;
    bt_device.device_id = "Device Address";
    bluetoothing_setmode(&bt_device);

    // Establish BLE connection
    bluetooth_t ble_device;
    ble_device.init();
    ble_device.connect("Device Address", NULL);

    return 0;
}
```
